    {page==='privacy'&&<section className="workspace privacy-page"><article className="privacy-document"><p className="eyebrow">LITTLE ARCHIVE · YOUR PRIVACY</p><h1>privacy <em>policy</em></h1><p className="privacy-updated"><strong>Last updated: October 27, 2026</strong></p><p>Welcome to <strong>Little Archive</strong> ! </p><p>Your privacy matters to us. Little Archive is designed to let you take photos, create photobooth strips, and save your favorite moments without requiring you to share personal information with us.</p><h2>1. Information We Collect</h2><p><strong>We do not intentionally collect personal information.</strong></p><p>Little Archive does not ask you to create an account, provide your name or email address, or submit personal details to use the photobooth.</p><h2>2. Photos and Images</h2><p>Your photos belong to you. </p><ul><li>Photos taken using the photobooth are processed within your browser.</li><li>We do not upload, collect, or store your photos on our servers.</li><li>We do not maintain a gallery or database of users' photos.</li><li>Your photos are not used for advertising, analytics, or training artificial intelligence.</li><li>You can choose whether to download or save your finished photobooth strips to your own device.</li></ul><p>Please note that downloaded images are saved to your device according to your browser's settings. Little Archive does not control how you manage those files afterward.</p><h2>3. Cookies and Tracking</h2><p>Little Archive does not intentionally use tracking cookies, advertising trackers, or analytics tools to monitor your activity.</p><p>However, our website's hosting provider or other technical services may process limited technical information as part of delivering and securing the website. Please refer to their respective privacy policies for details.</p><h2>4. Third-Party Services</h2><p>Little Archive may rely on third-party services to host and deliver the website. These providers may process technical information necessary to operate their services.</p><p>We do not intentionally send your photos or personal information to third parties. If you choose to share a downloaded photo through another application or service, that service's own privacy policy will apply.</p><h2>5. Data Storage and Security</h2><p>Little Archive does not maintain a server-side database of personal information or photographs.</p><p>Photos and temporary editing data may exist in your browser's memory while you use the photobooth. Closing or refreshing the page may clear this temporary data, depending on your browser and the website's implementation.</p><p>Because no online service can guarantee absolute security, we encourage you to use a trusted device and be mindful when saving or sharing personal photos.</p><h2>6. Children's Privacy</h2><p>Little Archive does not knowingly collect personal information from children or other users. The photobooth is intended to be used without providing personal details.</p><p>If you are a parent or guardian with a privacy concern, you may contact us using the contact information provided on our website.</p><h2>7. Your Privacy and Choices</h2><p>You remain in control of the photos you take and save. You can choose not to grant camera permission, stop using the photobooth at any time, and decide whether to download or share your images.</p><p>You can revoke camera access through your browser's site settings.</p><h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2><p>We may update this Privacy Policy when Little Archive's features or practices change. Any updates will be published on this page along with a revised “Last updated” date.</p><h2>9. Contact Us</h2><p>If you have questions or concerns about this Privacy Policy, email <a href="mailto:mikyla0888@gmail.com">mikyla0888@gmail.com</a>.</p><button className="text-link privacy-back" onClick={home}>← back to the cover</button></article></section>}
